  <page_number>34</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Non</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Tunc omne terris omnibus heu genus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Mortale tantis imbribus obrutum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Una periisset forte, passim</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Victima nil miserantis unda.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">
      <i>Sed vir relictus coniuge cum pia est,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Cultor supremi numinis integer,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Arca capaci clausus aluo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Cum genitis nuribúsque charis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9" para="true">
      <i>Successit istis orta parentibus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Terras per omnes gens habitabiles</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Diffusa, Sol quacunque Mundum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Limpidus irradiat patentem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13" para="true">
      <i>Lugenda chordis flebilibus mala,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Irata summi dextera Iudicis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Quae mittit, ut poenas nefandis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Criminibus meritas rependat.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17" para="true">
      <i>Concussa motu Gallia civico</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Paces quietas odit, &amp; ocia</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Vicina turbat, quin ruinam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Dum ruit ipsa alys minatur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21" para="true">
      <i>Sic tecta tectis finitimis metus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Incensa magnos protinus afferunt,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Casura sic damnum propinquis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Arboribus meditatur arbos.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25" para="true">
      <i>Nec sola bello Gallia concidit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Sed dira cunctos cladibus horridis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Bellona mortales fatigat,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Funeribúsq; cruentat orbem.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The first word of the page is set with a large initial "T", read as "Tunc". The running head is set in small capitals and read as printed. The "q;" in "Funeribúsq;" is a doubtful reading of the abbreviation sign; it is kept as printed and not marked. The printed "alys" and "nuribúsque" are read as printed. The long s is written as plain s throughout. The verse is treated as one paragraph per sentence, as the stanza breaks are not otherwise marked.</notes>
